## Migration Workflow

### Standard Migration Process

Every page follows this workflow from legacy to modern architecture:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PHASE 1: ANALYSIS                                               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Study legacy WebForms page (.aspx + .aspx.vb)               │
│ 2. Extract business rules and calculations                      │
│ 3. Identify UI components and interactions                      │
│ 4. Map data structures and validation rules                     │
│ 5. Identify API endpoints needed                                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PHASE 2: REACT MIGRATION                                        │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Create TypeScript type definitions                           │
│ 2. Create React functional component with hooks                 │
│ 3. Implement UI (preserve visual identity)                      │
│ 4. Add data-testid to ALL interactive elements                  │
│ 5. Implement responsiveness (mobile, tablet, desktop)           │
│ 6. Implement accessibility (WCAG AA)                            │
│ 7. Create CSS Module for styling                                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PHASE 3: BACKEND INTEGRATION                                    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Create API service layer (axios)                             │
│ 2. Implement React Query hooks (useQuery, useMutation)          │
│ 3. Connect component to hooks                                   │
│ 4. Implement loading, error, and success states                 │
│ 5. Test integration with backend APIs                           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PHASE 4: TESTING (100% COVERAGE REQUIRED)                      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Create Vitest test file (.test.tsx)                          │
│ 2. Test rendering and UI components                             │
│ 3. Test user interactions (clicks, inputs, forms)               │
│ 4. Test filters and cascading dropdowns                         │
│ 5. Test data loading (async with waitFor)                       │
│ 6. Test CRUD operations                                          │
│ 7. Test business rule validations                               │
│ 8. Test accessibility (labels, ARIA, keyboard)                  │
│ 9. Test responsiveness (3 breakpoints)                          │
│ 10. Test error handling and edge cases                          │
│ 11. Achieve 100% test coverage (MANDATORY)                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PHASE 5: QUALITY ASSURANCE                                      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Run all tests (npm test) - 100% must pass                    │
│ 2. Run linter (npm run lint) - 0 errors allowed                 │
│ 3. Run formatter check (npm run format:check)                   │
│ 4. Verify accessibility with audit tools                        │
│ 5. Test on real devices (mobile, tablet, desktop)               │
│ 6. Code review by team member                                   │
│ 7. Update documentation and checklist                           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            ↓
                      ✅ COMPLETE
```

